  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Credit guarantee risk premium USAID/Banco Terra</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Kreditgar riskpremie USAID/Banco Terra</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In September 2011, Sida entered into a co-guarantee agreement with USAID/DCA (Development Credit Authority, now DFC) and Banco Terra. The risk has been shared equally between the two guarantors (25% each) and the guaranteed amount was 2 278 963 USD respectively (set to an equivalent of 22 800 000 SEK for Sida).
The loan guarantee was designed to strengthen the guaranteed party&#xb4;s - Banco Terra - ability to finance loans to medium-sized farm, agribusiness and tourism enterprises in Mozambique, through reducing the credit risk of defined lines of credit. A&#xa0;particular focus on woman owned enterprises was intended. Increased lending by Banco Terra to agribusinesses and tourism MSMEs (medium, small, and micro entreprises) should thereby stimulate economic growth as borrowers use the loan capital to expand productive capacity. The loan guarantee activities are national in scope, with special concentration on the Beira and Nacala corridors and the southern zone of Mozambique (the bank can lend anywhere, but borrowers cannot be located in Maputo City).</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Risk premium reg a credit guarantee that Sweden is providing together with USAID and Banco Terra in order to increase the number of credits to emerging farmers.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Riskpremie r&#xf6;rande kreditgaranti som Sverige st&#xe4;llt till f&#xf6;rfogande   tillsammans med USAID och Banco Terra f&#xf6;r att &#xf6;ka utl&#xe5;ningen till     medelstora b&#xf6;nder.</narrative>
  </description>
